{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "Q9EV94", "secondaryAccessions": ["E3PXR7"], "uniProtkbId": "GRDE_ACESD", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "2006-06-13", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2025-02-05", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2001-03-01", "entryVersion": 81, "sequenceVersion": 1}, "annotationScore": 3.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Acetoanaerobium sticklandii (strain ATCC 12662 / DSM 519 / JCM 1433 / CCUG 9281 / NCIMB 10654 / HF)", "commonName": "Clostridium sticklandii", "taxonId": 499177, "lineage": ["Bacteria", "Bacillati", "Bacillota", "Clostridia", "Peptostreptococcales", "Filifactoraceae", "Acetoanaerobium"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"value": "Glycine reductase complex component B subunits alpha and beta"}, "ecNumbers": [{"value": "1.21.4.2"}]}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"value": "Selenoprotein PB alpha/beta"}}], "contains": [{"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"value": "Betaine reductase component B subunit beta"}}}, {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"value": "Betaine reductase component B subunit alpha"}}}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"value": "grdE"}, "orderedLocusNames": [{"value": "CLOST_1110"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"}], "value": "In the first step of glycine reductase, the substrate is bound to component PB via a Schiff base intermediate. Then the PB-activated substrate is nucleophilically attacked by the selenol anion of component PA to transform it to a carboxymethylated selenoether and the respective amine. By action of component PC, acetyl phosphate is formed, leaving component PA in its oxidized state. Finally component PA becomes reduced by the thioredoxin system to start a new catalytic cycle of reductive deamination (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "acetyl phosphate + [thioredoxin]-disulfide + NH4(+) + H2O = [thioredoxin]-dithiol + glycine + phosphate + H(+)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:12232"}, {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA-COMP:10698"}, {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA-COMP:10700"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15377"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15378"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:22191"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:28938"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:29950"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:43474"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:50058"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:57305"}], "ecNumber": "1.21.4.2"}}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"}], "value": "Heterohexamer of two alpha, two beta and two gamma subunits. Component of the glycine reductase complex, together with components A and C. PB is substrate specific (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"}], "value": "The peptide chain is cleaved into beta and alpha chains, and the alpha chain N-terminal cysteine is deaminated and oxidized to form a reactive pyruvoyl group"}], "commentType": "PTM"}, {"texts": [{"value": "The protein sequence in PubMed:11422384 comes from protein overexpressed and processed in E.coli"}], "commentType": "MISCELLANEOUS"}], "features": [{"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 241, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Betaine reductase component B subunit beta", "featureId": "PRO_0000240008"}, {"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 242, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 430, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Betaine reductase component B subunit alpha", "featureId": "PRO_0000240009"}, {"type": "Active site", "location": {"start": {"value": 242, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 242, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Schiff-base intermediate with substrate; via pyruvic acid", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}]}, {"type"